# What must NOT go into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so everything not named here is baked in.
# That makes this file the whole boundary between the source and the artefact,
# and the cost of getting it wrong is paid on every build.

# ── Generated sites ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The file store. This is where every site a seller has generated lives - 50MB
# of it on this machine and growing with every generation. It is runtime state,
# not source: baking it in ships one machine's sellers to every deployment,
# and rebuilds the image whenever anyone generates anything.
local_store/

# Working directories the app creates for itself at boot (see api/server.py),
# so they are never needed in the image and their contents never are.
static/uploads/
static/generated/

# ── Environment & secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Injected at runtime. A key baked into an image is a key in every layer of it,
# recoverable long after it is deleted from the file.
.env
*.key

# ── Python cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bytecode compiled against a different Python than the image runs.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# ── Development only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
requirements-dev.txt
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by people, not by the service. Named one by one rather than as *.md,
# because skills/ is full of .md files that ARE loaded at runtime by the art
# director, and whether a bare *.md reaches them depends on knowing that
# Docker's * does not cross a slash. The re-include below says it outright, so
# the next person to add a doc pattern cannot silently strip the agent's
# instructions and get a site rendered by the fallback rules instead.
README.md
prd.md
API_DOCUMENTATION.md
!skills/

# ── Git metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Editor & OS artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Docker files themselves ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
